    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Not available from EG4 cloud",
      "description": "What battery data the EG4 cloud does not provide for the 12000XP, and why.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 12
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "The EG4 cloud feed for the **12000XP** only reports bank-level battery values. These are **not provided**, so this dashboard does not show them:\n\n| Not available | Why |\n|---|---|\n| Per-cell voltages (min / max cell V, cell spread) | the cloud's battery endpoint returns no per-module array for this inverter |\n| Cell / battery temperatures | same, and the 12000XP's battery-temperature field is always empty |\n| State of health (SOH) | only reported per module, and there are no modules in this feed |\n| Cycle count | only reported per module; use *Lifetime battery throughput* as the wear indicator |\n| Per-module SOC, voltage, current, serial and firmware | no per-module data in the cloud feed |\n| Installed capacity and remaining Ah | not reported, so **usable energy remaining (kWh)** cannot be worked out without guessing the pack size |\n\n**Other things to know**\n- *Battery current* comes from a separate, slower EG4 battery endpoint and can lag the power readings.\n- History starts **2026-05-08** (install day). Data before 2026-09-26 18:26 was imported from the EG4 portal export at ~4-min resolution; after that it is recorded live (~2 min).\n- All data comes from the EG4 cloud (a new point every ~1-2 min, sometimes 5). A break in a line means no data, not zero.",
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        }
      }
    }
